    "result_text": "There's a single test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required a `checkDigit` field = a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`. I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property to the Owner schema (a read-only `int32`, range 0\u20139). Since `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec by the openapi-generator-maven-plugin at build time, this adds the field to the response DTO.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `checkDigit` plus a `checkDigit(Owner)` default method that computes the Luhn check digit over the digits in `customerCode` (ignoring the `<LAST3>-` prefix/separator), returning `null` when the customer code is absent. The algorithm mirrors the test's reference `luhn()` exactly (right-to-left, doubling starting at the rightmost digit, `(10 - sum % 10) % 10`).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` \u2014 which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact `checkDigit` \u2014 passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
